1. Definitions
--------------

1.1 "Non-Commercial User" means:

    (a) employees, students, faculty, and other personnel of not-for-
        profit research institutions, government laboratories, and
        universities, when conducting research that is NOT (i) a
        commercial service, or (ii) contract research or services for
        a for-profit company where the intellectual property resulting
        from such research or service is owned, controlled, or
        primarily benefits such for-profit company; and

    (b) individuals, EXCLUDING (i) any use by, for, or on behalf of an
        entity organized for profit, and (ii) any use intended for or
        directed toward commercial advantage or monetary compensation.

1.2 "Non-Commercial Purpose" means use of the Software solely for
    internal academic research, teaching, personal study, or other
    activities that qualify under Section 1.1, in each case where no
    monetary compensation, commercial advantage, or commercial
    benefit is sought or obtained, directly or indirectly.

1.3 "Commercial Use" means any use of the Software that is not a
    Non-Commercial Purpose, including without limitation:

    (a) use by, on behalf of, or for the benefit of a for-profit
        entity;
    (b) use in the development, training, evaluation, deployment, or
        provision of any product, service, pipeline, model, or tool
        that is sold, licensed, offered as a service (including
        software-as-a-service, model-as-a-service, or API access),
        or otherwise made available for a fee or other monetary
        consideration;
    (c) use to generate, design, validate, or optimize molecules,
        proteins, sequences, or other assets that are used in a
        commercial product, clinical pipeline, or fee-bearing service;
    (d) use within or in support of contract research, consulting, or
        fee-for-service work, including academic fee-for-service work
        whose intellectual property is owned by or assigned to a for-
        profit entity; and
    (e) integration of the Software into any commercial software,
        platform, or workflow.

1.4 "Modifications" means any changes to, additions to, or derivative
    works based upon the Software, including modified source code,
    fine-tuned or distilled model weights that materially rely on the
    Software, and translations or ports of the Software.


